      "snapshot": "Short Range Forecast Discussion\nNWS Weather Prediction Center College Park MD\n218 PM EST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nValid 00Z Mon Nov 16 2026 - 00Z Wed Nov 18 2026\n\n...Snow across the Rockies...\n\n...Rain across the Western and Central Gulf Coast into early\nMonday...\n\n...Rain and snow downwind from the Great Lakes through Sunday\nevening...\n\nAn upper-level trough will slowly move away from the Northeast and\nproduce spotty higher-elevation snow across parts of New York\nState and New England, with lower-elevation rain through Sunday\nevening. In addition, some of the highest elevations of West\nVirginia will get wet snow through Sunday evening. High pressure\nwill move into the Ohio Valley by Monday and inching into the\nCentral Appalachians by Tuesday. The high pressure will create\nclear skies and calm wind across parts of the Southeast through\nTuesday.\n\nUpper-level energy over Texas will move eastward to the Southeast\nby Tuesday, producing rain with embedded thunderstorms over the\nSouthern Plains through Sunday evening. Showers will linger over\nthe Lower Mississippi Valley through late Monday morning. Easterly\nflow off the Atlantic will create scattered showers along the\nFlorida Coast and associated Gulf Coast Tuesday.\n\nMeanwhile, a front over the Northwest moves inland to the Rockies\nby Tuesday. The system will produce rain and higher-elevation snow\nover parts of the Northwest through Monday morning. Snow and\nlower-elevation rain will develop over the Northern Intermountain\nRegion into the western Rockies by Tuesday. Along with the front,\nsnow levels will lower over parts of the Northern Intermountain\nRegion and the Sierra Mountains in California, producing light\nsnow over the highest elevations on Sunday into Tuesday morning.\nThe snow has prompted Winter Weather Advisories over parts of the\nSierra Mountains through Tuesday.\n\n\n\nZiegenfelder\n\n\nGraphics available at\n<a href=\"https://www.wpc.ncep.noaa.gov/basicwx/basicwx_ndfd.php\"><u>https://www.wpc.ncep.noaa.gov/basicwx/basicwx_ndfd.php</u></a>"
    },
